              "metric": "SC-2",
              "severity": "SEVERE",
              "description": "Orphaned Task at line 422: `bridge.onActivity = { Task { await vm.loadMessages() } }`. This `Task { }` is created from the `bridge.onActivity` callback (an arbitrary escaping closure), NOT directly inside the SwiftUI `.task` modifier body, so the SwiftUI exception does not apply. The Task handle is not stored, has no cancellation path, and may fire after the view disappears or be retained beyond its useful scope. Store the handle (or refactor `loadMessages` callback to a structured AsyncStream/AsyncSequence consumed within the `.task` body) and cancel it on disappear/detach.",
